{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changing","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stream","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SsfStreamV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changes","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfStreamInput","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14SsfStreamInputV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfStreamInput","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14SsfStreamInputV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let stream = try await client.ssf.getStream(streamID: id)","let body = SsfStreamInput.changing(stream) { $0.eventsAllowed = [.sessionRevoked] }","_ = try await client.ssf.updateStream(streamID: id, body: body)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What the body carries, and why each point is a rule rather than a convenience:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventsRequested"},{"type":"text","text":", as read."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" An update that omits it ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resets"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the stream to every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event of ","type":"text"},{"code":"eventsAllowed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", widening what the receiver narrowed, and AXIAM then sends the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receiver more events about the tenant’s users than it asked for. The read list goes back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as it was; an ","type":"text"},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the receiver’s “none”) goes back as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and is never omitted.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cut to the new ceiling."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" lowers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventsAllowed"},{"type":"text","text":" and does not name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventsRequested"},{"type":"text","text":", the requested list becomes the entries of the read list that are in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventsAllowed"},{"type":"text","text":", in their order (a request outside the ceiling is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"400"},{"type":"text","text":"). An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventsRequested"},{"type":"text","text":" that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" sets to anything other than what was read — a list, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" (absent: a reset) — is sent as given: the server judges it. Setting it to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"very value that was read is the same as not naming it, and is cut like the rest. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differs from §32.2 read literally, which would send a value set to the one read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given (the server then answering "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"400"},{"type":"text","text":" if it lies outside the new ceiling): here the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cut is applied instead, which is benign. To send the read list uncut, build the body"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput\/init(copying:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and edit it yourself."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectedUpdatedAt"},{"type":"text","text":", as read."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"updatedAt"},{"type":"text","text":" string of the stream you read, byte for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"byte — never parsed and rendered again, because the comparison is of the instant and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timestamp rounded to fewer fraction digits than the server stored does not match. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"update then lands only on the version you read, and a write made since (the receiver’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own included) answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"409"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConflictError"},{"type":"text","text":", never retried): read again and decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again. Setting it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" is “none”: the key is left out of the body and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is never sent, which replaces whatever is stored."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The header.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"authorizationHeader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"clearAuthorizationHeader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" start ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(absent keeps the stored header, §32.2); set them in ","type":"text"},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the update moves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to another origin (§32.3 rule 5).","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput\/init(copying:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the plain converter, and the cut is the caller’s duty there."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput\/changing(_:_:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfStreamInput"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"changing"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SsfStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SsfStreamV"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","